# Patch 0004: conversation replay on attach (ACP session/load).
#
# Applied last, on top of 0001..0003. Paseo keeps agent timelines in daemon
# memory, so after a daemon restart the only surviving copy of a conversation is
# the dsh session log on disk. The bridge advertised only session/resume, which
# re-attaches without replaying anything, and Paseo's ACP client replays history
# exclusively on the loadSession branch -- so every resumed dsh agent opened
# with an empty chat even though its transcript was intact.
#
# initialize now advertises agentCapabilities.loadSession, and session/load
# resumes the persisted session and re-sends its transcript as session/update
# notifications before answering (Paseo collects updates only while its load
# request is in flight). The live event-to-update mapping moved into
# translateSessionEvent so streaming and replay share one implementation, and
# assistant chunks now carry the dsh message id, which is what Paseo groups a
# message's chunks by. The replay skips assistant/chunk deltas, because the
# assistant/message closing the step carries the same text, and adds the user
# turns the live path never echoes.
#
# session/resume is unchanged: a side chat still attaches without history, and
# Paseo marks its history primed so the inherited parent context stays hidden.

